# ─ Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Tooling caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ── Local scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anything a developer wants to keep out of the research record goes here, so it
# is never confused with canonical state.
.cache/
.scratch/
*.local.json

# ── Large research payloads ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model weights and raw corpora are never canonical repository state. What is
# canonical is the manifest and the freeze that pins their bytes by digest. If a
# payload is deleted, the freeze still records what it was, and verification
# reports the artifact as missing rather than quietly passing.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.h5
*.onnx
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment capture redacts secret-shaped variables (see docs/PROVENANCE.md),
# but a stray .env must never be committed in the first place.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json